1
00:00:29,900 --> 00:00:35,357
I'll see you

2
00:00:35,440 --> 00:00:39,680
next time.

3
00:01:56,900 --> 00:01:57,877
who'd been wounded.

4
00:01:57,960 --> 00:02:01,237
When we fixed him up, he couldn't
believe we were being so nice to him.

5
00:02:01,320 --> 00:02:03,197
Things seem fairly quiet for a change.

6
00:02:03,280 --> 00:02:05,574
Of course, quiet never lasts long here.

7
00:02:18,380 --> 00:02:19,210
Who's that?

8
00:02:21,280 --> 00:02:23,104
Hey, don't you come any closer.

9
00:02:23,240 --> 00:02:24,593
Wait, I won't hurt you.

10
00:02:24,940 --> 00:02:26,157
Do we believe you?

11
00:02:26,240 --> 00:02:27,400
He sounds familiar.

12
00:02:29,560 --> 00:02:31,240
Wait, I don't trust him.

13
00:02:31,380 --> 00:02:33,097
Don't give me any of your job, baby.

14
00:02:33,180 --> 00:02:35,356
Come out, come out, wherever you are.

15
00:02:35,880 --> 00:02:37,397
I'll explain everything later.

16
00:02:37,480 --> 00:02:39,715
Right now, we need to get out of here.

17
00:02:43,280 --> 00:02:44,240
Hey, wait up.

18
00:02:44,440 --> 00:02:47,322
Don't leave me here with
this whacked out monkey.

19
00:02:52,820 --> 00:02:55,177
Supreme, I'm fired up and
ready to go on a main street.

20
00:02:55,260 --> 00:02:58,020
Slow down, you four-footed giant furball.

21
00:02:58,460 --> 00:03:01,497
This is certainly more convenient
than waiting for a taxi.

22
00:03:01,580 --> 00:03:04,797
If I'd known we were gonna go
riding, I'd have worn long pants.

23
00:03:04,880 --> 00:03:05,710
Me too.

24
00:03:05,793 --> 00:03:06,623
I need a side saddle.

25
00:03:06,706 --> 00:03:08,778
This place doesn't look very lively.

26
00:03:09,900 --> 00:03:11,220
It's kinda spooky.

27
00:03:13,460 --> 00:03:14,440
Look up there.

28
00:03:16,860 --> 00:03:18,540
I think I'm gonna barf.

29
00:03:19,420 --> 00:03:22,217
That's the restaurant where
they made me work like a slave.

30
00:03:22,300 --> 00:03:25,597
I'm still trying to get that greasy
spoon smell out of my sweater.

31
00:03:25,680 --> 00:03:27,060
But this is all wrong.

32
00:03:27,240 --> 00:03:29,005
It's supposed to be Nero Lake.

33
00:03:32,800 --> 00:03:33,917
Everything's changed.

34
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:35,577
Hurry, we'd better find shelter.

35
00:03:35,660 --> 00:03:37,160
This place is depressing.

36
00:03:37,520 --> 00:03:39,932
There's not even a clean chair to sit on.

37
00:03:44,540 --> 00:03:45,370
Awesome!

38
00:03:45,453 --> 00:03:47,597
Leomon, you are not going
to believe what you missed.

39
00:03:47,680 --> 00:03:49,360
I can't believe it's you!

40
00:03:49,800 --> 00:03:53,557
I am truly happy to have finally
returned and helped my friends.

41
00:03:53,640 --> 00:03:54,522
You digivolved.

42
00:03:55,320 --> 00:03:57,497
A lot has happened to me since being set

43
00:03:57,580 --> 00:04:00,227
free of the Black Gears
and their evil power.

44
00:04:03,320 --> 00:04:06,967
Being exposed to the Digivice
has now enabled me to Digivolve.

45
00:04:07,440 --> 00:04:09,420
But there is one problem. Huh?

46
00:04:09,820 --> 00:04:11,620
I am unable to control it.

47
00:04:11,920 --> 00:04:13,557
I haven't learned the secret yet.

48
00:04:13,640 --> 00:04:14,897
It's all still new to me.

49
00:04:14,980 --> 00:04:18,156
What makes you special, you
oversized doggy, Chew Toy?

50
00:04:18,320 --> 00:04:21,297
Let's just see how many
lives you have left. Huh?

51
00:04:21,380 --> 00:04:22,210
Huh?

52
00:04:24,600 --> 00:04:25,440
Dirty cat!

53
00:04:30,140 --> 00:04:32,557
There is nothing more
pathetic than a whiner.

54
00:04:32,640 --> 00:04:35,522
Clearly you don't deserve
to be called a Digimon.

55
00:04:42,700 --> 00:04:43,582
Who's in there?

56
00:04:43,720 --> 00:04:44,550
Show yourself!

57
00:04:46,220 --> 00:04:48,757
The last thing we want
to do is cause trouble!

58
00:04:48,840 --> 00:04:50,117
Oh, Palmon, look!

59
00:04:50,200 --> 00:04:53,200
They delivered the triple
hot fun sundae. Huh?

60
00:04:53,440 --> 00:04:55,700
Wow, the princess would look! Huh?

61
00:04:56,420 --> 00:04:58,240
Princess Meadie, yippee!

62
00:05:03,940 --> 00:05:04,920
Take that!

63
00:05:06,760 --> 00:05:07,920
Here he comes!

64
00:05:08,820 --> 00:05:10,700
Oh, no! He's back!

65
00:05:10,880 --> 00:05:12,586
Well, we are shooting at him!

66
00:05:12,960 --> 00:05:16,177
I bet they don't invite Puppetmon
to their birthday parties.

67
00:05:16,260 --> 00:05:20,554
I think it's a good thing that they're
finally releasing their hostility.

68
00:05:22,060 --> 00:05:23,160
Get out now!

69
00:05:28,380 --> 00:05:30,677
You guys know you're not allowed upstairs.

70
00:05:30,760 --> 00:05:33,800
My room is off-limits, but
I hate sharing my time.

71
00:05:34,140 --> 00:05:37,257
I'd say that you need to learn a
little more about good manners.

72
00:05:37,340 --> 00:05:39,928
We're not hurting
anything except maybe you.

73
00:05:40,500 --> 00:05:42,157
We've had it with you, Puppet Mon.

74
00:05:42,240 --> 00:05:43,070
You're toast.

75
00:05:43,480 --> 00:05:44,857
Oh, now you want to play, huh?

76
00:05:44,940 --> 00:05:47,175
How about a game of follow the leader?

77
00:05:48,080 --> 00:05:50,340
Come back here, you cutie toothpick.

78
00:05:50,460 --> 00:05:52,754
You play with us and you're gonna lose.

79
00:05:58,440 --> 00:05:59,880
Huh? It's a trick.

80
00:06:00,140 --> 00:06:01,380
Not our best move.

81
00:06:02,900 --> 00:06:03,960
Well, putt punk.

82
00:06:04,320 --> 00:06:06,360
See, TJ, I have friends after all.

83
00:06:06,540 --> 00:06:08,422
Problem is, they don't like you.

84
00:06:11,200 --> 00:06:13,494
And what they don't like, they destroy.

85
00:06:14,300 --> 00:06:15,137
Kill us!

86
00:06:15,220 --> 00:06:18,240
Red Vegiemon have
extremely volatile tempers,

87
00:06:18,360 --> 00:06:22,419
that's why their faces are always
red, not exactly the friendly type.

88
00:06:24,980 --> 00:06:27,020
It's time to do some wig-whacking!

89
00:06:27,240 --> 00:06:28,457
How come you two were hiding?

90
00:06:28,540 --> 00:06:30,246
What happened to your palace?

91
00:06:30,800 --> 00:06:34,624
The palace was completely destroyed
by those creepy Dark Masters!

92
00:06:34,780 --> 00:06:36,160
Yeah, it was horrible!

93
00:06:36,520 --> 00:06:38,217
They attacked just for the fun of it!

94
00:06:38,300 --> 00:06:40,057
We all had to run for our lives!

95
00:06:40,140 --> 00:06:43,457
We were all separated and we've
been hiding here ever since!

96
00:06:43,540 --> 00:06:44,370
How awful!

97
00:06:44,453 --> 00:06:46,020
Those guys make me sick.

98
00:06:46,120 --> 00:06:49,797
Who do they think they are, anyway,
picking on poor, defenseless Digimon?

99
00:06:49,880 --> 00:06:51,140
I mean, is that fair?

100
00:06:51,480 --> 00:06:54,951
The Darkmasters have to be
stopped if we expect to survive.

101
00:06:55,840 --> 00:06:59,117
I've spent all this time searching
for you, but it hasn't been easy.

102
00:06:59,200 --> 00:07:01,057
The Darkmasters have seen to that.

103
00:07:01,140 --> 00:07:03,557
You two have the power
to defeat those beasts,

104
00:07:03,640 --> 00:07:07,477
but you must work together and join
forces with the other Digidestined.

105
00:07:07,560 --> 00:07:09,300
Only then will you succeed.

106
00:07:09,920 --> 00:07:13,273
Are you saying we wasted our
time fighting everyone else?

107
00:07:13,780 --> 00:07:17,192
I mean, I could have stained
my clothes with perspiration.

108
00:07:17,940 --> 00:07:18,840
Listen, girly.

109
00:07:19,060 --> 00:07:21,297
If you would have fought
those guys at the start,

110
00:07:21,380 --> 00:07:24,900
you would have broken way
more than just a sweat. Maybe.

111
00:07:25,480 --> 00:07:27,417
But what about the good Digimon on File

112
00:07:27,500 --> 00:07:30,147
Island that sacrificed
themselves to help us?

113
00:07:31,280 --> 00:07:32,110
Mimi.

114
00:07:32,200 --> 00:07:33,100
This is true.

115
00:07:33,420 --> 00:07:34,277
What do you mean?

116
00:07:34,360 --> 00:07:36,297
I think you were brought to File Island to

117
00:07:36,380 --> 00:07:38,577
prove that you were capable
of working as a team.

118
00:07:38,660 --> 00:07:42,477
It could have been a test to make
sure that you were the Digidestined.

119
00:07:42,560 --> 00:07:44,440
Did we pass? You did.

120
00:07:44,700 --> 00:07:46,112
It actually makes sense.

121
00:07:46,260 --> 00:07:50,097
If Devimon had defeated you, then you would
not be ready for this bigger challenge.

122
00:07:50,180 --> 00:07:53,077
Devimon's power was nothing
compared to the Dark Masters.

123
00:07:53,160 --> 00:07:54,807
He was merely the beginning.

124
00:07:55,540 --> 00:07:57,697
But you've proven yourselves over and over

125
00:07:57,780 --> 00:08:00,177
by defeating one evil
Digimon after another.

126
00:08:00,260 --> 00:08:02,672
You're ready to take on the Dark Masters.

127
00:08:03,080 --> 00:08:05,845
Come on, we must find
your friends immediately.

128
00:08:05,960 --> 00:08:07,725
So tell me, where did they go?

129
00:08:07,820 --> 00:08:09,317
We can't do this all alone.

130
00:08:09,400 --> 00:08:11,697
Some of us needed a
timeout from each other.

131
00:08:11,780 --> 00:08:12,797
You know how it is.

132
00:08:12,880 --> 00:08:14,200
You needed a timeout?

133
00:08:15,180 --> 00:08:17,886
Yeah, you might say it's
another kind of test.

134
00:08:20,740 --> 00:08:21,720
Meteor away!

135
00:08:27,080 --> 00:08:28,021
Electroshockers!

136
00:08:30,320 --> 00:08:31,200
And a bait!

137
00:08:33,980 --> 00:08:34,980
Lightning pop!

138
00:08:36,200 --> 00:08:40,017
You guys are not as useful as a
load of stinky rotten vegetables.

139
00:08:40,100 --> 00:08:41,335
I've had it with you!

140
00:08:41,780 --> 00:08:42,610
Huh?

141
00:08:42,693 --> 00:08:44,780
Try to stop us now! Digimon!

142
00:08:44,920 --> 00:08:48,140
Pokémon, one Digimon! Turn! Digimon!

143
00:08:48,420 --> 00:08:51,008
Digital monsters, Digimon
are the champions!

144
00:08:51,600 --> 00:08:52,430
Digimon!

145
00:08:52,560 --> 00:08:55,148
Digital monsters, Digimon
are the champions!

146
00:09:01,480 --> 00:09:02,310
Digimon!

147
00:09:05,080 --> 00:09:05,910
Digimon!

148
00:09:06,080 --> 00:09:08,668
Digital monsters, Digimon
are the champions!

149
00:09:11,780 --> 00:09:12,920
Poor Greymon!

150
00:09:16,160 --> 00:09:17,440
Terra Force!

151
00:09:18,960 --> 00:09:20,240
Perfect Power!

152
00:09:23,520 --> 00:09:24,840
Think you're so smart?

153
00:09:24,940 --> 00:09:26,116
Nobody toys with me!

154
00:09:30,640 --> 00:09:32,480
He's got me strung up!

155
00:09:33,660 --> 00:09:35,440
The enemy's that way!

156
00:09:35,820 --> 00:09:36,720
Poor Greymon!

157
00:09:37,200 --> 00:09:38,357
Don't come too close!

158
00:09:38,440 --> 00:09:40,499
I don't know what it'll make me do!

159
00:09:41,940 --> 00:09:43,340
Oh, oh!

160
00:09:47,380 --> 00:09:48,210
Kari!

161
00:09:48,660 --> 00:09:49,490
Nijimam!

162
00:09:49,780 --> 00:09:50,610
OK, we won!

163
00:09:51,080 --> 00:09:52,580
Nijimam! Nijimam!

164
00:09:54,240 --> 00:09:56,300
Nijimam, get yourself, too!

165
00:09:57,380 --> 00:09:58,277
Nijimam, get yourself, too!

166
00:09:58,360 --> 00:09:59,948
Nijimam, get yourself, too!

167
00:10:01,260 --> 00:10:02,090
Nijimam!

168
00:10:02,320 --> 00:10:03,360
Oh my God!

169
00:10:04,300 --> 00:10:05,130
Gotcha!

170
00:10:07,600 --> 00:10:10,660
Keep running, kids, I
don't want to catch you!

171
00:10:18,520 --> 00:10:19,920
whoo

172
00:10:20,660 --> 00:10:21,920
kabuterimon digimon 2

173
00:10:28,660 --> 00:10:30,520
mega kabuterimon

174
00:10:57,900 --> 00:10:59,780
I'm not afraid of you.

175
00:11:02,080 --> 00:11:03,900
If I were you, I'd reconsider.

176
00:11:05,400 --> 00:11:06,920
Wait, we must be careful.

177
00:11:07,080 --> 00:11:08,786
The Digidestined are strong.

178
00:11:09,060 --> 00:11:10,537
Stronger than I suspected.

179
00:11:10,620 --> 00:11:14,237
Don't underestimate them, Puppet
Mon, or it could be disastrous.

180
00:11:14,320 --> 00:11:15,150
What?

181
00:11:15,233 --> 00:11:16,063
Spit it out already.

182
00:11:16,146 --> 00:11:17,957
Are you saying that I might lose?

183
00:11:18,040 --> 00:11:20,177
I'm only saying, take them seriously.

184
00:11:20,260 --> 00:11:22,597
The Digidestined have something you don't.

185
00:11:22,680 --> 00:11:24,117
What does he mean by that?

186
00:11:24,200 --> 00:11:26,259
I got more powers than I ever will.

187
00:11:26,520 --> 00:11:28,417
Fools, I'm never gonna lose to you.

188
00:11:28,500 --> 00:11:29,330
Watch.

189
00:11:34,840 --> 00:11:37,740
I know something you don't.

190
00:12:06,140 --> 00:12:07,440
It's showtime, baby!

191
00:12:12,180 --> 00:12:13,400
It's Metal Atamon.

192
00:12:13,540 --> 00:12:14,400
He never quit!

193
00:12:18,580 --> 00:12:20,557
You trying to pull a number on me, bro?

194
00:12:20,640 --> 00:12:23,377
I'm going to wait on the
line because I'm so fine.

195
00:12:23,460 --> 00:12:24,290
Deal with me.

196
00:12:24,373 --> 00:12:26,026
Then we shall see who's fine.

197
00:12:27,420 --> 00:12:28,780
Leomon Digimolk 2? Ooh!

198
00:12:29,580 --> 00:12:30,460
Saber Leomon!

199
00:12:32,040 --> 00:12:32,870
Whoa!

200
00:12:33,020 --> 00:12:34,897
Well, I see we've been
takin' our vitamins,

201
00:12:34,980 --> 00:12:36,997
but it's time to put the
cat out with the garbage.

202
00:12:37,080 --> 00:12:38,997
Saber Leomon may have a heart of gold,

203
00:12:39,080 --> 00:12:41,797
but he'll crush his opponents
with his claws of steel.

204
00:12:41,880 --> 00:12:42,820
Don't do it!

205
00:12:43,260 --> 00:12:44,297
I'll be all right.

206
00:12:44,380 --> 00:12:46,086
Now run before it's too late.

207
00:12:46,480 --> 00:12:47,480
Howling crushers!

208
00:12:56,460 --> 00:12:58,557
I'm not gonna sit here and watch this.

209
00:12:58,640 --> 00:13:00,100
Hey, guys, wait for me!

210
00:13:01,540 --> 00:13:02,370
Nijirun.

211
00:13:02,453 --> 00:13:03,283
Nijirun.

212
00:13:03,366 --> 00:13:04,720
Gamma Mons! Nijirun!

213
00:13:05,340 --> 00:13:06,170
To...

214
00:13:06,420 --> 00:13:07,250
Nijirun!

215
00:13:08,400 --> 00:13:11,300
Mimi, please let me fight with them! Well?

216
00:13:12,460 --> 00:13:14,320
They need me. What should I do?

217
00:13:15,120 --> 00:13:16,820
Mimi? Harpoon torpedo!

218
00:13:19,820 --> 00:13:20,650
Wait!

219
00:13:20,820 --> 00:13:22,077
What do you mean, wait?

220
00:13:22,160 --> 00:13:23,437
We've got to help him out!

221
00:13:23,520 --> 00:13:26,837
But don't you think it's a better
idea to leave like he told us to?

222
00:13:26,920 --> 00:13:27,750
But Joe!

223
00:13:28,640 --> 00:13:29,560
Twin fangs!

224
00:13:31,700 --> 00:13:32,530
What?

225
00:13:32,613 --> 00:13:34,977
I really think we'd better
leave before it's too late.

226
00:13:35,060 --> 00:13:36,119
What about Leomon?

227
00:13:37,080 --> 00:13:38,786
You call that your best shot?

228
00:13:39,500 --> 00:13:40,600
Metal punch!

229
00:13:43,400 --> 00:13:47,600
He's nothing if you want a real
challenge, it's right here. What?

230
00:13:48,040 --> 00:13:51,216
Ogremon, don't be ridiculous,
you're no match for him.

231
00:13:51,560 --> 00:13:54,678
Hey, listen, I can take on
this tin can if I want to.

232
00:13:55,020 --> 00:13:55,850
No!

233
00:13:56,300 --> 00:13:57,130
Mimi!

234
00:13:57,600 --> 00:13:59,137
You're in no shape to fight.

235
00:13:59,220 --> 00:14:01,597
Now stop it and quit trying to be a hero.

236
00:14:01,680 --> 00:14:03,033
No, everyone's welcome.

237
00:14:03,240 --> 00:14:06,837
As a matter of fact, little darling, today
I'm offering a special group discount.

238
00:14:06,920 --> 00:14:10,038
Besides, it saves me time
to destroy all you at once.

239
00:14:12,600 --> 00:14:13,500
Baby, no!

240
00:14:19,300 --> 00:14:20,720
Okay, that does it.

241
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:34,830
Ekakumon!

242
00:14:34,913 --> 00:14:36,340
Jigimon, Jigimon!

243
00:14:39,440 --> 00:14:40,270
Jigimon!

244
00:14:41,040 --> 00:14:42,400
End to ultamin'.

245
00:14:48,180 --> 00:14:49,220
Euro-mon!

246
00:14:52,040 --> 00:14:53,660
Leon-mon, wake up!

247
00:14:53,860 --> 00:14:55,625
Please tell me you're alright!

248
00:14:58,480 --> 00:15:00,892
As you can see, that didn't even faze me.

249
00:15:01,080 --> 00:15:04,357
My metal's Chromadigizoid, the
absolute strongest metal there is.

250
00:15:04,440 --> 00:15:06,028
Then maybe you'd like this.

251
00:15:06,220 --> 00:15:07,161
MULCAN'S HAMMER!

252
00:15:09,400 --> 00:15:11,812
No matter what you attempt, it's useless.

253
00:15:12,120 --> 00:15:13,460
Cuz I'm invincible.

254
00:15:16,120 --> 00:15:18,540
I'm breaking apart. This is terrible.

255
00:15:18,760 --> 00:15:19,760
I lost my luster.

256
00:15:19,860 --> 00:15:21,417
Why does this keep happening to me?

257
00:15:21,500 --> 00:15:23,977
Because my hammer is made
of Chromadigizoid metal.

258
00:15:24,060 --> 00:15:26,197
I'm afraid it isn't your moment to shine!

259
00:15:26,280 --> 00:15:27,160
That can't be!

260
00:15:27,580 --> 00:15:29,080
Twin Fang! Uh-oh.

261
00:15:35,060 --> 00:15:36,200
No pain, Victor!

262
00:15:39,320 --> 00:15:40,500
He did it!

263
00:15:44,480 --> 00:15:45,700
You man!

264
00:15:48,380 --> 00:15:51,820
Don't worry, I've got it
covered! Get moving! Ah!

265
00:15:53,420 --> 00:15:54,700
Cory, come on!

266
00:15:55,520 --> 00:15:56,350
Ah!

267
00:15:58,360 --> 00:15:59,190
No!

268
00:15:59,700 --> 00:16:00,820
Wind rain!

269
00:16:03,600 --> 00:16:04,920
It fizzled out!

270
00:16:06,120 --> 00:16:07,320
Mega Kabuterimon!

271
00:16:07,840 --> 00:16:09,080
TK, hurry, run!

272
00:16:09,280 --> 00:16:10,221
Okay, good luck!

273
00:16:12,760 --> 00:16:14,540
Ha-ha, I'm outta here!

274
00:16:14,660 --> 00:16:15,778
Happy housewarming!

275
00:16:16,120 --> 00:16:18,220
Take me too! Are you joking?

276
00:16:18,380 --> 00:16:19,837
Do I look like I want your company?

277
00:16:19,920 --> 00:16:20,750
Take this!

278
00:16:20,833 --> 00:16:21,920
Puppet cover!

279
00:16:31,340 --> 00:16:32,640
Who's that behind me?

280
00:16:32,840 --> 00:16:35,240
Well, it's about time! Get them!

281
00:16:35,380 --> 00:16:37,968
Do some major damage
and I want no fall-ups!

282
00:16:41,540 --> 00:16:42,370
Huh?

283
00:16:44,940 --> 00:16:45,881
What's with you?

284
00:16:45,980 --> 00:16:47,017
Daydreaming again, huh?

285
00:16:47,100 --> 00:16:47,930
Huh?

286
00:16:48,013 --> 00:16:49,020
No, Metal Karuru Mom!

287
00:16:49,220 --> 00:16:50,102
Sock it to him!

288
00:16:50,520 --> 00:16:51,877
Hey, this isn't working here.

289
00:16:51,960 --> 00:16:53,437
Remember, you're supposed to obey me.

290
00:16:53,520 --> 00:16:54,350
I'm the boy!

291
00:16:54,720 --> 00:16:55,580
Think again.

292
00:16:57,760 --> 00:16:59,357
You're washed up, Puppet Mom.

293
00:16:59,440 --> 00:17:02,777
Nobody's gonna be on your side
because you don't care about them.

294
00:17:02,860 --> 00:17:06,037
I'm still strong, and it
doesn't matter what they think.

295
00:17:06,120 --> 00:17:08,177
They're still gonna do
what I tell them to do!

296
00:17:08,260 --> 00:17:09,090
Ah!

297
00:17:10,360 --> 00:17:11,240
Metal Karuru!

298
00:17:20,400 --> 00:17:25,620
Cherrymon, what is it that those
kids have that I don't... Friends!

299
00:17:34,460 --> 00:17:35,780
Thank you, Matt!

300
00:17:36,800 --> 00:17:37,630
Huh?

301
00:17:49,840 --> 00:17:51,437
Outlet Pumenbun's been defeated!

302
00:17:51,520 --> 00:17:53,108
The forest is disappearing!

303
00:17:53,420 --> 00:17:54,250
Run!

304
00:17:54,333 --> 00:17:57,060
We've got to get out of
here and find a safe place!

305
00:18:03,760 --> 00:18:05,000
Lihuman, it's me!

306
00:18:05,180 --> 00:18:06,020
Come on now!

307
00:18:06,260 --> 00:18:07,100
Yeah, wake up!

308
00:18:07,660 --> 00:18:11,131
This stupid toilet paper isn't
gonna be any good this time!

309
00:18:13,480 --> 00:18:14,357
The forest...

310
00:18:14,440 --> 00:18:16,120
the forest is disappearing!

311
00:18:18,160 --> 00:18:21,042
It's a sign that something
positive has happened.

312
00:18:21,600 --> 00:18:25,120
Your friends must have defeated
Puppetmon. That's good.

313
00:18:25,340 --> 00:18:26,960
I expected that they would.

314
00:18:27,680 --> 00:18:29,437
Oh, Leomon, please don't leave us.

315
00:18:29,520 --> 00:18:30,540
We depend on you.

316
00:18:30,780 --> 00:18:32,427
You have no reason to worry.

317
00:18:32,700 --> 00:18:36,240
I must go now and rejuvenate
myself at the primary village.

318
00:18:36,880 --> 00:18:37,710
But...

319
00:18:37,980 --> 00:18:39,451
Ogremon, I'm very sorry.

320
00:18:39,840 --> 00:18:44,664
Now is not the time for us to resolve
things, but I promise we will meet up again.

321
00:18:44,980 --> 00:18:46,500
You're a good rival.

322
00:19:01,320 --> 00:19:03,820
Mimi, let's go to the primary village.

323
00:19:05,220 --> 00:19:08,280
Yes, we need help, and if
what Leomon said is true,

324
00:19:08,600 --> 00:19:10,377
we'll meet some old friends there.

325
00:19:10,460 --> 00:19:13,931
Wouldn't it be just great to
see Chuumon and Pixiemon again?

326
00:19:14,080 --> 00:19:15,437
Well, then the matter's settled.

327
00:19:15,520 --> 00:19:18,557
We're making a trip to find
the primary village, all right?

328
00:19:18,640 --> 00:19:19,937
There's only one problem.

329
00:19:20,020 --> 00:19:20,997
It doesn't exist.

330
00:19:21,080 --> 00:19:22,668
There isn't anything there.

331
00:19:22,880 --> 00:19:23,777
It's a ghost town.

332
00:19:23,860 --> 00:19:27,397
It was destroyed after the Dark
Masters poisoned it with their evil.

333
00:19:27,480 --> 00:19:28,540
No one is left.

334
00:19:28,760 --> 00:19:29,700
It can't be.

335
00:19:30,180 --> 00:19:34,709
It will never return to the way it was
until the Dark Masters are eliminated.

336
00:19:35,060 --> 00:19:35,920
Any ideas?

337
00:19:36,340 --> 00:19:39,281
I say we throw them out
and then save the village.

338
00:19:39,460 --> 00:19:40,457
That would be great.

339
00:19:40,540 --> 00:19:43,077
It's better than sitting
around and doing nothing.

340
00:19:43,160 --> 00:19:43,990
Okay, Mimi.

341
00:19:44,240 --> 00:19:47,697
The only way out of this mess
is to defeat the Dark Masters.

342
00:19:47,780 --> 00:19:48,610
Are you up for it?

343
00:19:48,693 --> 00:19:50,052
We need your help, Mimi.

344
00:19:50,180 --> 00:19:51,160
Please say yes.

345
00:19:51,340 --> 00:19:55,120
For Leomon and everyone, the
whole Digi-World needs us.

346
00:19:57,640 --> 00:19:58,997
Yes, you're right, Palmon.

347
00:19:59,080 --> 00:20:02,845
Sniveling is for babies, and I've
done too much of that already.

348
00:20:03,040 --> 00:20:05,687
Ogremon, are you going
to come along with us?

349
00:20:06,920 --> 00:20:07,750
Huh?

350
00:20:07,833 --> 00:20:11,057
Well, I have no intention of
joining forces with you crazy kids.

351
00:20:11,140 --> 00:20:15,611
However, if we all happen to be going
the same way, I'm stuck tagging along.

352
00:20:15,720 --> 00:20:16,777
Don't worry, Ogremon.

353
00:20:16,860 --> 00:20:17,777
We won't blow your cover.

354
00:20:17,860 --> 00:20:20,797
Now that it's decided, we
need to seek out a few allies.

355
00:20:20,880 --> 00:20:21,710
Allies?

356
00:20:21,793 --> 00:20:22,623
Where?

357
00:20:22,706 --> 00:20:23,697
There must be others
who are willing to fight

358
00:20:23,780 --> 00:20:25,857
the Dark Masters and
get their hands dirty.

359
00:20:25,940 --> 00:20:27,097
I know they're out there.

360
00:20:27,180 --> 00:20:29,177
We just have to find them, that's all.

361
00:20:29,260 --> 00:20:30,090
Yeah.

362
00:20:30,280 --> 00:20:35,280
Hey, Princess, how about if we come
along to help out? No way. Huh? Come on.

363
00:20:36,060 --> 00:20:39,707
Only if you stop calling me
Princess and call me Mimi instead.

364
00:20:40,380 --> 00:20:41,498
Our pleasure, Mimi.

365
00:20:41,600 --> 00:20:42,718
So can we come now?

366
00:20:43,220 --> 00:20:44,177
Of course you can.

367
00:20:44,260 --> 00:20:45,877
Some call this a crossroads in life.

368
00:20:45,960 --> 00:20:48,537
In the past, I might have
avoided it by going to the mall.

369
00:20:48,620 --> 00:20:50,917
But you know, it feels
good to do the right thing,

370
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:55,765
even though at times that might be a
dangerous thing, which we may soon find out.

371
00:21:19,060 --> 00:21:20,377
Thank

372
00:21:20,460 --> 00:21:21,777
you

373
00:21:21,860 --> 00:21:28,860
so

374
00:21:30,460 --> 00:21:31,937
much

375
00:21:32,020 --> 00:21:39,020
for

376
00:21:39,140 --> 00:21:39,970
watching.

377
00:21:40,053 --> 00:21:42,557
You will be stronger than

378
00:21:42,640 --> 00:21:45,237
one thing I

379
00:21:45,320 --> 00:21:49,837
am now with the

380
00:21:49,920 --> 00:21:55,697
courage to take the courage
To the heart of my heart,

381
00:21:55,780 --> 00:22:00,837
I can still see the future I am

382
00:22:00,920 --> 00:22:04,000
now with the future of the world

383
00:22:05,520 --> 00:22:09,060
It's still the beginning of the day

384
00:22:10,000 --> 00:22:10,830
It's a dream.

385
00:23:04,000 --> 00:23:05,680
Thank you.
